### 4.4 Upload the SCOS Image to OCI Object Storage

The SCOS image was uploaded to OCI Object Storage using Terraform.

The Terraform configuration contains separate modules for:

```text
terraform/modules/
├── object-storage/
└── custom-image/
```

The workflow is:

```text
SCOS QCOW2 Image
       │
       ▼
Terraform
       │
       ▼
OCI Object Storage
       │
       ▼
OCI Custom Image
```

The Object Storage module creates the bucket and uploads the SCOS image.

The Custom Image module imports the uploaded image into OCI as a reusable Compute image.

### Verify Object Storage

After Terraform completes:

```bash
oci os object list \
  --namespace-name "$NAMESPACE" \
  --bucket-name okd-images
```

Verify that the SCOS image is present:

```text
scos-10.0.20251103-0-openstack.x86_64
```

### Verify the Custom Image

```bash
oci compute image list \
  --compartment-id <COMPARTMENT_OCID>
```

Verify that the imported SCOS image is present and its lifecycle state is:

```text
AVAILABLE
```

### Verification Checklist

```text
[ ] Terraform created/managed the Object Storage resources
[ ] SCOS image exists in the okd-images bucket
[ ] Custom Image was created
[ ] Custom Image state is AVAILABLE
```

The SCOS image is now ready to be used as the boot image for the OKD nodes.